      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Manners let KYVALLEY RAY NZ (5) down on his return to Australia but he is much better than that as as a multiple Group 1 winner in NZ. The hitout should have done him good and he has won two of three previous second-up attempts so will have come on. Prepared to give him another chance. MUNNY THE MUNSTER (7) raced parked but dug deep to get home narrowly in his heat, his second success from his last three outings here. Cops a wider draw but he is good enough to make an impact with even luck. THE PREACHER (4) was just behind MUNNY THE MUNSTER in the heats and draws inside that rival this time. Contender. REVERAND BOB (2) draws well and must be respected off a narrow win in the heats while UNCLAD (8) was a touch disappointing last start but was going well prior and draws for a trail so could bounce back.",
